   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ ״וַיִּשְׁלַח יוֹאָב תְּקוֹעָה וַיִּקַּח מִשָּׁם אִשָּׁה חֲכָמָה״, מַאי שְׁנָא תְּקוֹעָה? אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: מִתּוֹךְ שֶׁרְגִילִין בְּשֶׁמֶן זַיִת, חָכְמָה מְצוּיָה בָּהֶן.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara notes the effect of Tekoa’s oil on those living there: The verse states: «“And Joab sent to Tekoa, and fetched from there a wise woman”» (II Samuel 14:2). «What is different» about «Tekoa» that Joab chose to bring a woman from there? «Rabbi Yoḥanan says: Since» the residents of Tekoa «are accustomed to» use «olive oil, wisdom is prevalent there.»"
  }
